==Battleground==
*3 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*2 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 30~40 seconds<sup>900f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dober P.D]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn, delay 23.33~33.33 seconds<sup>700f~1,000f</sup>.
**5 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Loris]] spawns.
**1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Dober and Jackrabbit are indeed threatening, but Puffingtons and the Relic peons will be the main pushers here, thanks to the former's dangerous Omni Strikes, high health, full backswing cooldown and extreme damage. The stage isn't quite over with their removal, so be prepared for a tough fight.

If you can manage to have Slime trade with the last Sir Rel and take him out, you can not only save up money indefinitely, but also use a kamikaze unit like Rock to hit the base, causing Puffington to rush ahead of the rest of the enemies. This makes him vulnerable to being nuked by Idi, taking him out early and relieving a lot of pressure.

Loris' presence shouldn't matter much, other than occasionally hitting units that are on the way.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] - Can Can is an incredibly efficient melee attacker with low cost and high stats, only hindered by single target. Paired with talents that grant increased speed and Extra Money, Can Can comfortably takes out most peons and can also greatly damage Puffington.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]] - A fast LD midranger with Massive Damage against Reds, Couriers can quickly remove Jackrabbits if and when they invade the frontline when meatshields cover its blindspot.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] - Having high speed and Extra Money, Bullet Train is a great general purpose attacker that can land at least one guaranteed hit. It is best used to snipe Jackrabbits.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]] - Idi's extreme burst damage against Relics is absolutely necessary in absence of a helpful Uber, and will come into use when fighting the second Puffington. Granted, she won't be able to finish him on her own without support, but removing him early makes the rest of the stage far easier.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando]] - An excellent anti-traitless midranger, Jagando's main highlights include his Strong, Knockback and level 1 Surge, helping to keep Dober in check once the other enemies have been dealt with. Even if Loris hits him, Jagando's Curse Immunity will keep his ability functional.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] - Best used during replays, Naala is Strong Against Relics, with 100% chance to weaken them to 50% for 4 seconds, alleviating the pressure of them on other units with far-reaching LD attacks. It also boasts Wave Immunity just in case if Dober fires one, and Jackrabbit falls to its mercy with Colossus Slayer.

